A program may set what a target reserves in its output block.

`reservedNames` is a const prop of the platform's build-target node like any
other option, and what the program writes replaces the platform's default for
that build: here bubbletea reserves `tally`, so the var is renamed, and none
of the names it reserves by default, so `cmds` is not.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `(?m)^\s+tally\s` -- the name the program reserved is renamed
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `cmds__r` -- a name only the replaced default reserved keeps its spelling

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import "sngl:platform/bubbletea"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea(reservedNames=["tally"])
    }
}

var tally = 0
var cmds = 0

window(title="tally") {
    button(text="{tally} {cmds}", @click {
        tally = tally + 1
        cmds = cmds + 2
    })
}
